  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.1.1 — Generated apps now pin the refreshed dependency set (Microsoft.* 10.0.15, OpenTelemetry 1.21.0, Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 6.1.8, Microsoft.OpenApi 2.13.1) and Asdamir.Core/Data 2.0.1, Web 2.3.1. No command or template behaviour changed. 2.1.0: `asdamir secrets check-gateways` proves every managed app's Gateway trusts a new signing key BEFORE the control plane switches to it (read-only; exit 0 only when all accept). The documented procedure for moving off the shared `Jwt:Key` changed with it: pin the new public key on each Gateway at step 1 (`Jwt:PublicKeyPem`), not `Jwt:JwksUrl` — see docs/secret-rotation.md. The generated `register_<app>.sql` now registers the app as centrally managed, so the control plane stops pushing localization/config edits to a Gateway that has no receiver. 2.0.0 notes (breaking for generated apps: Core/Data 2.0, no shared `Jwt:Key`, no default tenant) are in CHANGELOG.md.",
